# tool-gap-surfaces — the decision table (family contract in fixture.yaml; per-row intent below).
# One assert, five arms: the three surfaces the SHIPPED brief must declare (the review-body row is
# the fix), the contrast row proving the guard detects the base declaration's blind spot, and the
# fail-loud arm for a brief that lost the line. The emitter half of the round-trip is asserted on
# every row (the PROMPT interpolates ${TOOL_GAP_SURFACES}).
# id                             | world      | patch | env                                          | expect        | params
reader-reads-issue-comment       |            |       | SURFACE=issue-comments                       | reader-reads  | surface=issue-comments
reader-reads-pr-body             |            |       | SURFACE=pr-bodies                            | reader-reads  | surface=pr-bodies
reader-reads-pr-review-body      |            |       | SURFACE=pr-review-bodies                     | reader-reads  | surface=pr-review-bodies
base-brief-misses-review-body    | base-brief |       | SURFACE=pr-review-bodies BRIEF_NAME=README.md | reader-misses | surface=pr-review-bodies
brief-declares-none              | no-line    |       | SURFACE=pr-review-bodies BRIEF_NAME=README.md | reader-none   | surface=pr-review-bodies
